// iris -> Telegram Desktop palette
//
// Generated by iris. Do not edit; edit the shell's Templates/Iris/telegram.tdesktop-theme..
//
// Adapted from a Material You (matugen) tdesktop theme. iris exposes a smaller
// semantic palette, so the Material roles are folded down as follows:
//
//   background / surface_*_low..high -> bg / surface     surface_container_highest -> dim
//   on_background / on_surface       -> fg               on_surface_variant / outline -> dim
//   primary / on_primary             -> accent / bg      error / on_error -> red / bg
//   tertiary / secondary             -> green / yellow   inverse_primary -> syntax_keyword
//
// Load in Telegram: Settings -> Chat Settings -> Themes -> Edit theme, or just
// open the generated ~/.cache/iris/telegram.tdesktop-palette with Telegram.

